"mid-endgame-02":{"title":"Endgame · Checkmate 2","difficultyLabel":"Intermediate · estimated difficulty","goal":"Red to move. Checkmate in 4 moves.","nodes.n0.choices[0].reason":"The Horse retreats with check. The General cannot go to file 5 (the flying General rule) or retreat to the back rank (a Black Advisor is in the way), so it must move up to the third rank.","nodes.n0.watchOut":"This is Black's only reply.","nodes.n1.choices[0].reason":"A quiet move: the Horse jumps back right in front of the Black General to act as a screen. It threatens C9=4 (the Cannon shifts to file 4 with the Horse as its screen) with checkmate, because the General cannot go to file 5 (the flying General rule) or retreat (it would still be on the Cannon's line).","nodes.n1.watchOut":"Black can only drag things out with C7=5: the Cannon comes back to the central file to block the line between the Generals. Every other move loses at once to C9=4.","nodes.n2.choices[0].reason":"The Red General moves up and takes the Black Cannon: the line between the Generals is open again and the mating threat is still there. The Black Cannon is unprotected, so the General takes it safely.","nodes.n2.watchOut":"Every Black move loses to C9=4.","nodes.n3.choices[0].reason":"The Cannon on file 9 shifts to file 4 and checks with the Horse as its screen. The General cannot go to file 5 (the flying General rule) or retreat (it stays on the Cannon's line), and no piece can block or take the Horse, so it is checkmate.","source":"Built by the author (working backward), Pikafish + exhaustive proof","verification":"Solution reviewed by the author and compared with Pikafish outside the app; the app checks the rules and the checkmate; not reviewed by an expert.","assessment":"Material: Red is slightly better (a Cannon, a Horse and a Soldier against Black's Cannon and Soldier; Black still has Advisors and Elephants). The Black General has moved up to the second rank on file 6; the Red General on the second rank of file 5 uses the flying General rule to control the whole central file, so the Black General cannot step onto file 5. Red's Horse on file 5 is on the back rank next to Black's palace, and Red's Cannon on file 9 on the riverbank on the left flank can shift sideways to file 4.","idea":"Use a Horse check to push the General up to the third rank, retreat the Horse with a quiet move so it becomes the Cannon's screen, take the Black Cannon with the Red General to keep the flying General rule in force, and then shift the Cannon across for checkmate.","urgency":"This endgame needs technique: if Red is slow, Black brings an Advisor back to the middle of the palace and the Cannon back to defend, and Red's win becomes very hard to achieve. The nice point is that the Red General is also an attacker: the flying General rule locks the central file throughout the exercise."},
"mid-endgame-03":{"title":"Endgame · Checkmate 3","difficultyLabel":"Intermediate · estimated difficulty","goal":"Red to move. Checkmate in 4 moves.","nodes.n0.choices[0].reason":"Chariot takes Chariot with check. The General has nowhere to go (its own Horse and Advisor are in the way), so it must take the Chariot and step onto file 4.","nodes.n0.watchOut":"This is Black's only reply.","nodes.n1.choices[0].reason":"The Soldier on file 6 advances with check. It is protected by the Soldier on file 7, so the General cannot take it and must go back to file 5.","nodes.n1.watchOut":"This is Black's only reply.","nodes.n2.choices[0].reason":"A quiet move: the Soldier on file 7 advances to the back rank, ready to shift in next to the General. The Black General is boxed in by its own Horse and Advisor with no escape; Red threatens checkmate with P7=6.","nodes.n2.watchOut":"Every Black move loses to P7=6. If the Horse jumps away to make an escape point, that point is still covered by the Soldier on file 6.","nodes.n3.choices[0].reason":"The Soldier shifts in with check. It is protected by the Soldier on file 6, the second-rank point is covered by the Soldier on file 6, and the file 6 point is blocked by a Black Advisor, so it is checkmate.","source":"Built by the author (working backward), Pikafish + exhaustive proof","verification":"Solution reviewed by the author and compared with Pikafish outside the app; the app checks the rules and the checkmate; not reviewed by an expert.","assessment":"Material: nearly level (Red has a Chariot and 3 Soldiers across the river; Black has a Chariot, a Horse, both Advisors and 2 Soldiers). Red's Chariot on file 9 is being attacked along the back rank by Black's Chariot on file 4 (R4=1). The Black General on the back rank of file 5 is surrounded by its own pieces: the Horse on file 5 on the second rank in front, the Advisor on file 6 on the back rank beside it. Two Red Soldiers (the one on file 7 on the second rank and the one on file 6 on the third rank) are pressing on the palace.","idea":"Trade Chariots to pull the General to file 4, check with the Soldier on file 6 to push it back, then play a quiet Soldier move to the back rank and mate with a Soldier: the Black General is smothered by its own pieces.","urgency":"The Red Chariot is under attack. Retreating it (R9-2) keeps an advantage but does not finish the game, and Black slowly deals with the two Red Soldiers; slower still, Black takes the Chariot and wins. Red must strike while the Black General is boxed in by its own pieces."},
"mid-endgame-04":{"title":"Endgame · Win material 1","difficultyLabel":"Intermediate · estimated difficulty","goal":"Red to move. Win material in 3 moves.","nodes.n0.choices[0].reason":"A quiet move: the Horse on file 4 retreats and attacks Black's Cannon on file 5. Black chooses to counterattack: the Cannon retreats to take the Soldier on file 5 with check.","nodes.n0.watchOut":"If Black plays A5+4, H6+5 takes the Cannon with check and Red is clearly ahead. If H7+6 checks, then K5+1, and Red still wins the Cannon.","nodes.n1.choices[0].reason":"The Horse on file 7 takes the Cannon: out of check and winning back material. Red has 2 Horses against Black's 1 Horse.","nodes.n1.watchOut":"Getting out of check with A6+5 leaves the game level.","nodes.n2.choices[0].reason":"The Horse pulls back: the Black General has just retreated to the back rank right next to the Horse, so a Horse that stays would be taken by the General. The Horse goes back to safety, and Red is a full Horse up.","nodes.n2.watchOut":"Do not leave the Horse on the back rank (for example A6+5): the Black General takes it and the endgame is level again.","source":"Pikafish self-play game (checked at 800k nodes per move)","verification":"Solution reviewed by the author and compared with Pikafish outside the app; the app checks the rules and the material at the end of the line; not reviewed by an expert.","assessment":"Material: a level endgame (Red has 2 Horses, 2 Soldiers and 2 Advisors; Black has a Cannon, a Horse, both Advisors and one Elephant). The Black General has moved up to the second rank on file 6. Red's Soldier on file 5 has reached Black's back rank but is targeted by Black's Cannon on file 5 (with an Advisor as its screen). Red's Horse on file 7 is on the second rank in Black's half and the Horse on file 4 is on the riverbank; Black's Horse on file 7 has crossed the river and threatens to jump in with check.","idea":"One quiet Horse move attacks Black's Cannon on file 5; Black takes a Soldier with check to escape, Red takes the Cannon with the Horse on file 7 (getting out of check and winning material at once), and then pulls the Horse back to safety: a piece up in the endgame.","urgency":"If Red is slow, Black's Horse on file 7 jumps in with check (H7+5) and then takes a Red Horse, and Red loses the endgame. This exercise asks you to calculate that losing a Soldier to a check still works out in Red's favor."},
